  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** QuidelOrtho’s results show a sharp contrast between a solid prior quarter and a difficult first quarter of 2026, driven almost entirely by an exceptionally weak respiratory season. Point-of-care testing demand cratered as influenza-like illness visits plummeted, while lab revenue also softened. Distributor destocking ahead of anticipated national IVD pricing guidelines introduced further near-term caution. On a more positive note, the company is advancing product launches in the U.S. and internationally and has acquired LEX Diagnostics to accelerate growth in point-of-care molecular diagnostics, signaling a push beyond seasonal respiratory reliance.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership acknowledged the respiratory headwind and lowered full-year guidance, disappointing the market after a large earnings miss. The team is actively reshaping the portfolio through the LEX Diagnostics acquisition and new product introductions, aiming to build a higher-growth molecular diagnostics franchise. However, the abrupt guidance cut and the magnitude of the quarterly shortfall have strained management’s credibility, as the business remains heavily exposed to volatile respiratory seasons despite strategic efforts to diversify.",
